For every smooth closed real $(1,1)$-form $q$, $$\begin{aligned}
 \mathcal Ld(F_t)&=\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}(B(0)^*k(x)B(0)),\label{eq:hessian-central}\\
 \mathcal LP_q(F_t)&=\frac1{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}
      (\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}_h q)(f(e^{i\theta}))\,\mathrm d\theta,\label{eq:hessian-poisson}\\
 \mathcal LA_h(F_t)&=n-A_{R_h}(f).\label{eq:hessian-area}
\end{aligned}$$ Here $F_t$ means the disc $z\mapsto F(t,z)$, not a parameter derivative.

outputs.exact_statement:
Let $h$ be a smooth Hermitian metric on $X$. There exist a number $p_0$ with $2<p_0\le p$ and a holomorphic frame $B=(b_1,\ldots,b_n)$ of $f^*T^{1,0}X$ which is continuous, nonsingular, and $W^{1,p_0}$ on $\overline\mathbb D$, such that $$\label{var:boundary-unitary}
 B(z)^*h(f(z))B(z)=I,
 \qquad z\in\partial\mathbb D.$$

Let $B$ and $p_0>2$ be as in Proposition <a href="#var:frame" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="var:frame">9</a>, and set $x=f(0)$. For some $\eta>0$, there is a map $$F\colon\{t\in\mathbb C^n:|t|<\eta\}\times\overline\mathbb D\longrightarrow X$$ which is continuous on its domain and jointly holomorphic on $\{|t|<\eta\}\times\mathbb D$, and satisfies $$\label{var:spray-identities}
 F(0,z)=f(z),\qquad F(t,0)=x,\qquad
 \frac{\partial F}{\partial t_j}(0,z)=z b_j(z).$$ In fixed local target coordinates covering the graph of $f$, the maps $t\mapsto F(t,\cdot)$ are holomorphic with values in $W^{1,p_0}$ on the corresponding source patches. In particular every $F(t,\cdot)$ is a finite-area holomorphic disc centered at $x$.

For every smooth closed real $(1,1)$-form $q$, $$\begin{aligned}
 \mathcal Ld(F_t)&=\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}(B(0)^*k(x)B(0)),\label{eq:hessian-central}\\
 \mathcal LP_q(F_t)&=\frac1{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}
      (\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}_h q)(f(e^{i\theta}))\,\mathrm d\theta,\label{eq:hessian-poisson}\\
 \mathcal LA_h(F_t)&=n-A_{R_h}(f).\label{eq:hessian-area}
\end{aligned}$$ Here $F_t$ means the disc $z\mapsto F(t,z)$, not a parameter derivative.
